    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d22">

                <pb facs="0029" n="17" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg17"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">121.840 Welles, Sumner/127: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Belgium</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Cudahy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-03-15T16:00:00-05:00">March 15, 1940—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>34. Your 60, March 14, 6 p.m. Department is requesting Paris to repeat to you
                    text of memorandum handed to Reynaud by Mr. Welles. It is understood that Mr.
                    Welles delivered same memorandum to other Governments he visited. The Department
                    is contemplating a more comprehensive communication to the states in
                        consultation.<anchor n="24" xml:id="d22-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
